Because it reminds of Cuiá
A friend or colleague there can expand and complete the list of projects that could be built with the R$ 122.4 million. Feel free. Just do a Google search and start gathering the values of large-scale projects that could be financed with the mountain of money that would be the change from the land swap.
As for the comparison with Cuiá (or the reminder of) is because this land business reminded me of that other one involving an area of permanent preservation that was expropriated and indemnized for R$ 11 million last year, on the eve of the election, by PMJP.
On the Cuiá land, according to specialists in Environmental Law, the City Hall didn't have to spend a single real because APPs (Areas of Permanent Preservation) are indemnizable, that is, strictly speaking, even within a private property, they cannot be altered or traded by the owner. They cannot be bought or sold, nor can they be expropriated and indemnized by the public power.
