II – This Commission's Competence
Article 32 of the Internal Regulation of the Chamber of Deputies outlines the thematic fields or areas of activity for each Standing Committee.

According to subparagraph XIV of this article, the thematic fields or areas of activity for the Committee on Mines and Energy are:

a) Brazilian mineral and energy policies and models;
b) the institutional structure and role of agents in the mineral and energy sectors;
c) conventional and alternative energy sources;
d) research and exploration of mineral and energy resources;
e) forms of access to mineral resources; mining companies;
f) energy resource pricing policy and structure;
g) commercialization and industrialization of minerals;
h) promotion of mining activity;
i) the legal regime of mineral resources and energy resources;
j) management, planning and control of water resources; legal regime of public and private waters.

Subparagraph "b", concerning the institutional structure and role of agents in the mineral and energy sectors, has a direct connection with PFC No. 97, as the ANP is the national regulatory body for the oil sector, responsible for collecting financial compensations resulting from oil and natural gas exploration.

Furthermore, the unique paragraph of Article 32, stating that the thematic fields or areas of activity for each Standing Committee encompass related governmental bodies and programs, as well as their budget monitoring, also allows the Committee on Mines and Energy to oversee the ANP.

III – Opportunity and Convenience
