IV – Legal, Administrative, Political, Economic, Social, and Budgetary Scope
From a legal and administrative perspective, there are benefits to be gained from implementing this proposal. An investigation with this scope can identify shortcomings, quantify potential losses, and point to responsible parties for corrective actions.
Other beneficial effects may result from this proposed regulatory action. Regulatory action undertaken under the auspices of the Legislative Power can correct any deviations and irregularities.
V – Execution Plan and Assessment Methodology
The execution plan for the legislative investigation subject to PFC No. 29 should include the following points:
– Determining the volumes of natural oil and gas produced in the country;
– Collecting the values of royalties and special participation charged by ANP for the exploitation of these natural resources;
– Determining the total royalties and special participation actually collected;
– Collecting the total due and the total transferred to each State and Municipality;
– Verifying the compatibility between the collected total and the transferred total;
– In case of discrepancies, requesting information and explanations from the involved authorities;
– Assessing the provided information and explanations and taking appropriate measures;
– Evaluating the criteria used by ANP for defining the municipalities eligible for royalties and special participation and the amounts transferred.
This PFC will be more effective if it employs an assessment methodology with continuous interaction with the involved bodies. Therefore, meetings and visits to the Ministry of Mines and Energy, the Ministry of Finance, and ANP will be necessary.
VI – Relator’s Vote
The aforementioned parliamentary initiative is undoubtedly commendable. It identifies the desire to benefit Brazilian municipalities particularly, through the proper collection, collection, and transfer of resources from royalties and special participation resulting from the exploitation of oil and natural gas.
